// WHAT poll_cast ANSWERS. These ARE the engine's VoteResult (src/engine/poll/PollBook.ts) and the
// correspondence is the contract between the two files - a number here that drifts from the enum
// there means the clerk cheerfully tells somebody their vote went in when it did not.
//
// ^poll_unavailable is -1 rather than 4 because it is not a result the database gave: it is the
// database not answering at all, which the op decides before it ever gets that far.
^poll_cast = 0
^poll_already = 1
^poll_closed = 2
^poll_badoption = 3
^poll_notyet = 4
^poll_unavailable = -1

// The widest menu content has is ~p_choice5, so five is the most options a poll can be ASKED with
// in game. tools/server/poll.ts refuses to post more than this for that reason - a sixth option
// would be invisible here while being perfectly votable on the website, which is the worst of both.
^poll_max_options = 5

// HOW LONG AN ACCOUNT MUST HAVE PLAYED BEFORE IT MAY VOTE, in minutes. Two hours.
//
// WHY TIME AND NOT IDENTITY. The worry is a poll being decided by accounts made that morning, and
// on a small player base that is a real worry. An account here is free and instant - there is no
// email on it - so one vote per account is no barrier at all; and keying votes on a linked Discord
// account only raises the price to one throwaway email, which is ten minutes' work. Hours cannot be
// bought that way. Old School gates its own polls the same way, on total level and hours played.
//
// It also costs nobody their vote: no Discord account, no launcher, the same in the browser client,
// and every real player passes it in an evening.
//
// MIRRORED IN TWO OTHER PLACES - POLL_MIN_MINUTES in the engine (src/engine/poll/PollService.ts)
// and MIN_MINUTES on the website (src/lib/polls.ts). Three programs ask the question and none of
// them can call the others. Raise it in all three, or the clerk and the website will disagree about
// who may vote. The clerk reads the engine's copy through poll_minminutes rather than this one, so
// this exists for anything content-side that wants the number without an op.
^poll_min_minutes = 120
